(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether the Bharat’s preparation of playing “FIFA world cup” tournament comes under the vision of Viksit Bharat 2047;
(b) the strategic preparations made for qualifying “FIFA world cup” under the Mission; and
(c) the details of roadmap taken by the Ministry for encouraging football in the country under the Mission?

(a) whether the Ministry has the policy of plantation, beautification along with maintenance of the National Highways across the country;
(b) the project implemented so far under the policy, if any, including project cost in the National Highways falling in Assam;
(c) the details thereof; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether the Ministry has declared new National Highway in Assam in the last three years and the impact of National Highway in the Assam's economic perspective;
(b) whether the Ministry has proposal to declare/construct New National Highway stretching from Jomduar in Kokrajhar district to Bhairabkunda in Udalguri district along the Indo-Bhutan borderline in Assam;
(c) if so, the details thereof; 
(d) if not, the reason therefor; and
(e) the present status of the construction of fly-over where NH-31c connects with NH-31 at Rakaldubi, Assam with financial status?

(a) the objectives of establishing Pradhan Mantri Bhartiya Janaushadhi Pariyojana (PMBJP);
(b) whether the Ministry has conducted health and socio-economic impact assessment on the contribution after the operation of this scheme;
(c) the numbers of PMBJP Kendras operational in Assam, district-wise;
(d) whether it is a fact that there is a huge trust deficit towards generic medicines in the country;
(e) whether there is any accountable monitoring agency on the operation of Janaushadhi Kendras at the district administrative level throughout the country, if so, the details thereof; and
(f) if not, the reason therefor?

(a) the impact and visibility of branding of Ashtalakshmi Mahotsav 2024 in NER tourism perspective; 
(b) the initiative taken by Government to mobilize investments for tourism development in NER; 
(c) whether Government has mapped the tourism circuits of National Parks in Assam to facilitate tourists to visit under one package; and
(d) the numbers of Domestic Tourist Visit (DTV) and Foreign Tourist Visit (FTV)to the national park in Assam during the years 2023, 2024 and 2025 including contribution of revenue thereof, National park-wise?

(a) whether it is a fact that funds have not been released for the post-matric scholarship of tribal students of Assam since 2023;
(b) the amount sanctioned and released for the post-matric scholarship of tribals students of Assam during last five years; and
(c) whether the Ministry is planning to increase the amount of post-matric scholarship per student considering the upsurge of daily expenditure of students, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the transformative initiatives to modernise inland water transport facilities in the North-Eastern States with special focus in the mighty river Brahmaputra in the State of Assam;
(b) whether the Ministry is planning to develop river cruise tourism in the North-Eastern States of India;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) if not, the reason therefor?

(a) whether the Ministry is planning to establish trade facilitation centre in the Indo-Bhutan border areas of the State of Assam to generate livelihood for the people living in border areas;
(b) whether the Ministry has received proposal from the State Government of Assam for the establishment of Border Haats across the Indo-Bhutan Border in Assam;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government is planning to develop tourism in tribal areas (Ethnos Tourism) in the country; 
(b) if so, the details of initiatives taken therefor, with special reference to the North-Eastern Region; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether the Ministry has taken special measures for strengthening health care system at the grass-root level in the sixth schedule areas of the country;  
(b) the impact of health programmed run by the Ministry in the sixth scheduled areas with special focus  to the higher prevalence of sickle cell, Anemia, malnutrition, communicable diseases like malaria etc.;
(c) if so, the details thereof in Sixth Scheduled States, area-wise; and
(d) if not, the reason therefor?

(a) whether Government is aware of prevalence of bonded labour in the country;
(b) if so, the numbers of such labourers identified, State-wise; and
(c) the details of steps taken to eradicate it, State-wise?

(a) whether the Ministry has  the present status of providing land entitlement to the landless people under the Forest Right Act, 2006 in Assam;
(b) whether the Ministry has achieved the objectives of FRA, 2006 meant for ensuring sustainable livelihood for the tribal communities and other forest dwellers across the country;
(c) if so, the details thereof; and 
(d) if not, the reason therefor?

(a) the positive impact of Deendayal Upadhyaya Grameen Kaushal Yojna under NRLM; 
(b) the outcome of providing placement-linked skill training to poor households in rural area;
