(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the quantum of fund sanctioned and released against each project for the years 2022, 2023 and 2024, if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has received project proposal of fifteen hundred crore from Bodoland Territorial Council of Assam under special package which was agreed to in the Bodo Accord signed in 2020;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the quantum of fund sanctioned and released against the each project by the Ministry so far, if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government is aware of the rising burden of stroke cases and if so, the magnitude of the same, which is posing public health challenges in the country;
(b) whether Government has achieved the desired level of objectives of the National Programme for Prevention and Control of Cancer, Diabetes, Cardiovascular Diseases and Stroke (NPCDCS);
(c) if so, the details thereof; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government is planning to step up exploration of mineral commodities including oil and Natural gas in the North Eastern States;
(b) the critical mineral commodities explored in the North-Eastern States in the years 2022, 2023, 2024;
(c) the quantum of fund sanctioned, released and spent for mineral exploration in the North-Eastern States, project-wise in the year 2022, 2023, 2024;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the annual project proposal received from the State Government of Assam for the development of International Border with Bhutan under Border Area Development Programme (BADP) for the years 2022, 2023 and 2024;
(b) the quantum of fund allocated/ released under BADP to the Assam Government during the last three years;
(c) whether the BADP has been able to create sense of security among the people of border areas by enhancing employment opportunities and by creating alternative avenues for earning;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a)  whether the Ministry of Jal Shakti has received proposals   for the critical flood control and anti-erosion schemes in Brahmaputra and Barak Valleys, from the State of Assam under Flood Management Program (FMP) of the Ministry;
(b)  if so, scheme-wise details of fund sanctioned and released for the year 2020, 2021, 2022 and 2023; and
(c)  if not, reasons therefor?

(a) whether the Ministry has taken projects for resolution of man-elephant conflicts in Assam which occur frequently in the elephant habitants’ zone, including Bodoland area;
(b) if so, the measures taken by Government for zero man-elephant conflict;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) whether measures were undertaken to promote conservation of tigers in the Manas National Park, Assam under the Project Tiger during the years 2021, 2022 and 2023; and
(e) if so, the details thereof, year-wise, if not, the reason therefor?

(a) whether Government has taken policy and project for flood management in the Indo-Bhutan transborder rivers i.e. Sonkosh, Aie, Manas, Beki, Pagladiya and Puthimari in the State of Assam under the Flood Management and Border Areas Programme (FMBAP) and River Management activities and works related to Border Areas (RMDA);
(b) if so, details of the policies and scheme undertaken in the last four years i.e.,  2020, 2021, 2022, 2023; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

